@startuml SALUD_Pay_Module_72_pay_ledger
title Module 72 — pay-ledger: Libro mayor (lo que TigerBeetle no guarda)\n(schema: pay_ledger)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide circle

' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
' PERFIL PAY (D-18). Una base de PostgreSQL POR SERVICIO: este módulo describe la base `pay_ledger`,
' no un schema de la base de SALUD. Se genera con salud-db/gen_ddl_pay.py a SQL/pay/72_pay_ledger/ (objetos sin
' calificar: se crean en el esquema de la conexión). Portado el 2026-10-27 del DDL de referencia de
' services/pay-ledger/sql/ (pasarelapago). A partir de acá la fuente de verdad es ESTE archivo.
' SQL de referencia de pay-ledger (P2.H1.M2). A mover a mantra-core-health-model (D-18): el modelo todavía no existe.
' TigerBeetle guarda saldos y asientos; acá vive lo que TigerBeetle no tiene (H-7 del spike): a qué operación de
' negocio corresponde cada asiento, el extracto y el rastro de los rechazos (H-2). Montos en centavos de BOB (bigint).
' Las tablas técnicas outbox_events / inbox_events / idempotency_keys vienen de contracts/packages/{outbox,idempotency}/sql.
' ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
note as BIZ_diagram_72_pay_ledger
  BUSINESS PURPOSE
  Base propia del microservicio pay-ledger de la pasarela de pagos ALOVIDA (libro mayor (lo que TigerBeetle no guarda)).
  Separación (regla #1 del plan maestro): ningún otro servicio lee estas tablas; los datos de otros
  servicios llegan por eventos o por sus APIs. Dinero en unidades menores enteras (amount_minor, BOB).
end note

' Modo (D-28): `test` o `live`, el de la CLAVE que hizo la petición (cabecera X-Pay-Mode). Cada registro lo lleva y toda consulta lo filtra; las cuentas
' de TigerBeetle también son distintas por modo (el id lo incluye), así que ni el saldo ni un asiento pueden mezclar `test` con `live`.
' Cuentas lógicas del plan de cuentas (PLAN-MAESTRO §3.3) y su id determinista de 128 bits en TigerBeetle.
entity ledger_accounts {
  * mode : text <<PK>>
  * account : text <<PK>>
  * kind : text
  ' hex del id de 128 bits
  * tb_id : char(32)
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

' Un asiento por (business_ref, attempt). Los rechazados también quedan: son los que fijan el siguiente attempt (H-TB1).
entity ledger_transactions {
  ' tx_<base> (el modo forma parte de la base)
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * business_ref : text
  * attempt : integer
  ' sha256 del contenido canónico: mismo attempt con otro contenido ⇒ 422
  * content_hash : char(64)
  * status : text
    reject_code : text
  * currency : char(3)
  * legs : jsonb
  * created_at : timestamptz
}

' Cada pata asentada (una transferencia de TigerBeetle). `id` es el tf_ que viaja en el evento ledger.transfer.posted.
entity ledger_legs {
  ' tf_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * source : text
  ' tx_… o hd_…
  * source_id : text
  * business_ref : text
  * attempt : integer
  * leg_index : integer
  * debit_account : text
  * credit_account : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * code : text
  * posted_at : timestamptz
}

' Extracto: dos líneas por pata (débito y crédito). Orden estable: (posted_at desc, id desc).
entity ledger_statement_lines {
  ' sl_<base>
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * account : text
  * leg_id : text <<FK>>
  * business_ref : text
  * attempt : integer
  * leg_index : integer
  * direction : text
  * counterparty_account : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
  * code : text
  * posted_at : timestamptz
}

' Retenciones (primera fase) con vencimiento.
entity ledger_holds {
  ' hd_<base> (el modo forma parte de la base)
  * id : text <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * business_ref : text
  * attempt : integer
  * content_hash : char(64)
  * status : text
    reject_code : text
  * debit_account : text
  * credit_account : text
  * amount_minor : bigint
    posted_amount_minor : bigint
  * currency : char(3)
    void_reason : text
  * expires_at : timestamptz
  * created_at : timestamptz
    resolved_at : timestamptz
}

' Rastro de rechazos (P2.H1.M9): TigerBeetle NO guarda las transferencias rechazadas (H-2 del spike).
entity ledger_rejections {
  * id : bigserial <<PK>>
  * mode : text
  * kind : text
  * business_ref : text
  * attempt : integer
  * reject_code : text
  ' nombre del estado de TigerBeetle (sin datos personales)
  * tb_status : text
  ' X-Service-Id
  * caller : text
  * rejected_at : timestamptz
}

' Tablas técnicas de @pay/outbox. Cada servicio las tiene en SU base. Se declaran en el modelo (D-18).
' Tabla técnica de @pay/outbox: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity outbox_events {
  ' id del CloudEvent; también es el Nats-Msg-Id
  * id : uuid <<PK>>
  ' orden de publicación
  * seq : bigserial
  * aggregate_type : text
  * aggregate_id : text
  * type : text
  ' tema NATS destino
  * subject : text
  ' el CloudEvent completo
  * envelope : jsonb
  * created_at : timestamptz
    published_at : timestamptz
  * attempts : integer
    last_error : text
}

' Tabla técnica de @pay/outbox: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity inbox_events {
  ' qué consumidor procesó el evento
  * consumer : text <<PK>>
  * event_id : text <<PK>>
  * processed_at : timestamptz
}

' Tabla técnica de @pay/idempotency. Cada servicio la tiene en SU base (regla de separación #1).
' Se declara en el modelo (mantra-core-health-model, D-18) y se aplica por el pipeline; este archivo es la referencia.
' Tabla técnica de @pay/idempotency: la declara la librería y cada servicio la tiene en SU base.
entity idempotency_keys {
  ' quién: el id del comercio
  * scope : text <<PK>>
  ' la Idempotency-Key del cliente
  * key : text <<PK>>
  ' sha256 de método + ruta + cuerpo canónico
  * request_hash : text
  * state : text
  ' hasta dónde llegó la ejecución
  * recovery_point : text
    response_status : integer
    response_body : jsonb
  ' null = nadie la está ejecutando
    locked_at : timestamptz
  ' identifica a quien la ejecuta (compare-and-set)
    lock_token : text
  * created_at : timestamptz
  * expires_at : timestamptz
}

ledger_statement_lines }o--|| ledger_legs : leg_id

entity "INDEXES · ledger_accounts" as idxset_ledger_accounts <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_accounts : (mode, account) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK ledger_accounts_tb_id_unique : (tb_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
ledger_accounts .. idxset_ledger_accounts : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · ledger_transactions" as idxset_ledger_transactions <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_transactions : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK ledger_transactions_ref_attempt_key : (mode, business_ref, attempt) UNIQUE BTREE
}
ledger_transactions .. idxset_ledger_transactions : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · ledger_legs" as idxset_ledger_legs <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_legs : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK ledger_legs_source_index_key : (source_id, leg_index) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX ledger_legs_business_ref_idx : (mode, business_ref, attempt) BTREE
}
ledger_legs .. idxset_ledger_legs : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · ledger_statement_lines" as idxset_ledger_statement_lines <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_statement_lines : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX ledger_statement_lines_account_page_idx : (mode, account, posted_at DESC, id DESC) BTREE
}
ledger_statement_lines .. idxset_ledger_statement_lines : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · ledger_holds" as idxset_ledger_holds <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_holds : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK ledger_holds_ref_attempt_key : (mode, business_ref, attempt) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX ledger_holds_pending_expiry_idx : (expires_at) BTREE WHERE status = 'pending'
}
ledger_holds .. idxset_ledger_holds : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · ledger_rejections" as idxset_ledger_rejections <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_ledger_rejections : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK ledger_rejections_ref_attempt_kind_key : (mode, kind, business_ref, attempt) UNIQUE BTREE
}
ledger_rejections .. idxset_ledger_rejections : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · outbox_events" as idxset_outbox_events <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_outbox_events : (id) UNIQUE BTREE
  UK outbox_events_seq_key : (seq) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX outbox_events_pending_idx : (seq) BTREE WHERE published_at IS NULL
}
outbox_events .. idxset_outbox_events : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · inbox_events" as idxset_inbox_events <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_inbox_events : (consumer, event_id) UNIQUE BTREE
}
inbox_events .. idxset_inbox_events : indexed by

entity "INDEXES · idempotency_keys" as idxset_idempotency_keys <<INDEX_SET>> {
  PK pk_idempotency_keys : (scope, key) UNIQUE BTREE
  IX idempotency_keys_expires_at_idx : (expires_at) BTREE
}
idempotency_keys .. idxset_idempotency_keys : indexed by

entity "PAY EXTRAS · pay_ledger" as pay_extras_pay_ledger <<PAY_EXTRAS>> {
  ' Lo que el generador base (gen_ddl.py) no expresa: defaults no booleanos, identidades, CHECK, FK compuestas,
  ' funciones, triggers y datos semilla. Lo materializa salud-db/gen_ddl_pay.py (05_constraints.sql / 06_seed.sql).
  DEFAULT ledger_accounts.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL ledger_accounts : ledger_accounts_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_accounts : ledger_accounts_kind_check | kind IN ('merchant_pending', 'merchant_available', 'merchant_debt', 'user_wallet', 'platform_fees', 'connector_clearing', 'payout_clearing', 'schedule_reserve')
  DEFAULT ledger_transactions.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL ledger_transactions : ledger_transactions_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_transactions : ledger_transactions_attempt_check | attempt >= 1
  CHECK_SQL ledger_transactions : ledger_transactions_status_check | status IN ('posted', 'rejected')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_transactions : ledger_transactions_reject_code_check | reject_code IN ('insufficient_funds', 'validation_failed')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_transactions : ledger_transactions_reject_consistency | (status = 'rejected') = (reject_code IS NOT NULL)
  DEFAULT ledger_legs.posted_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_source_check | source IN ('transaction', 'hold')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_leg_index_check | leg_index >= 0
  CHECK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_amount_minor_check | amount_minor > 0
  FK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_debit_account_fkey | (mode, debit_account) -> ledger_accounts (mode, account)
  FK_SQL ledger_legs : ledger_legs_credit_account_fkey | (mode, credit_account) -> ledger_accounts (mode, account)
  CHECK_SQL ledger_statement_lines : ledger_statement_lines_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_statement_lines : ledger_statement_lines_direction_check | direction IN ('debit', 'credit')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_statement_lines : ledger_statement_lines_amount_minor_check | amount_minor > 0
  ' Las dos cuentas de una retención deben existir en ledger_accounts, como las de una pata (revisión de seguridad 2026-10-28). Compatible con el
  ' servicio: hold.service.ts#createHold llama a AccountRegistry.register(client, mode, [debit, credit]) DENTRO de la misma transacción y ANTES de
  ' cualquiera de los dos INSERT INTO ledger_holds (el aceptado y el rechazado); ningún otro código escribe en ledger_holds.
  FK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_debit_account_fkey | (mode, debit_account) -> ledger_accounts (mode, account)
  FK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_credit_account_fkey | (mode, credit_account) -> ledger_accounts (mode, account)
  FK_SQL ledger_statement_lines : ledger_statement_lines_account_fkey | (mode, account) -> ledger_accounts (mode, account)
  DEFAULT ledger_holds.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_attempt_check | attempt >= 1
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_status_check | status IN ('pending', 'posted', 'voided', 'expired', 'rejected')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_reject_code_check | reject_code IN ('insufficient_funds', 'validation_failed')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_amount_minor_check | amount_minor > 0
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_posted_amount_minor_check | posted_amount_minor >= 0
  CHECK_SQL ledger_holds : ledger_holds_void_reason_check | void_reason IN ('requested', 'downstream_failed')
  DEFAULT ledger_rejections.rejected_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL ledger_rejections : ledger_rejections_mode_check | mode IN ('test', 'live')
  CHECK_SQL ledger_rejections : ledger_rejections_kind_check | kind IN ('transaction', 'hold')
  DEFAULT outbox_events.created_at : now()
  DEFAULT outbox_events.attempts : 0
  DEFAULT inbox_events.processed_at : now()
  DEFAULT idempotency_keys.recovery_point : 'started'
  DEFAULT idempotency_keys.created_at : now()
  CHECK_SQL idempotency_keys : idempotency_keys_state_check | state IN ('started', 'completed')
  FUNCTION forbid_mutation
  | CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION forbid_mutation() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
  | BEGIN
  |   RAISE EXCEPTION 'la tabla % es inmutable (%)', TG_TABLE_NAME, TG_OP USING ERRCODE = 'integrity_constraint_violation';
  | END;
  | $$
  ' Registros de SOLO-AGREGAR del libro mayor (CLAUDE.md reglas 5 y 11: los errores se corrigen con asientos inversos, nunca con UPDATE ni DELETE). Hasta ahora lo
  ' cumplía el código y NO la base: `UPDATE ledger_legs SET amount_minor = …` a mano pasaba. Evidencia de que el servicio solo hace INSERT (grep en services/*/src, test/ y e2e/):
  ' ledger_transactions ledger.service.ts#INSERT; ledger_legs ledger.service.ts#INSERT; ledger_statement_lines ledger.service.ts#INSERT; ledger_rejections ledger.service.ts y
  ' hold.service.ts#INSERT; ninguna sentencia UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE ni INSERT … ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE sobre ellas. NO se guarda `ledger_holds` (máquina de estados:
  ' pending -> posted/voided/expired) ni `ledger_accounts`. UPDATE/DELETE por fila y TRUNCATE por sentencia (que no pasa por los triggers de fila); DROP SCHEMA/DROP TABLE de las
  ' bases descartables de prueba no se ven afectados. Mismo SQLSTATE (23000) y mensaje que forbid_mutation() de pay_merchants/pay_risk/pay_connectors.
  TRIGGER ledger_transactions_immutable : BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON ledger_transactions FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_transactions_no_truncate : BEFORE TRUNCATE ON ledger_transactions FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_legs_immutable : BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON ledger_legs FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_legs_no_truncate : BEFORE TRUNCATE ON ledger_legs FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_statement_lines_immutable : BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON ledger_statement_lines FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_statement_lines_no_truncate : BEFORE TRUNCATE ON ledger_statement_lines FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_rejections_immutable : BEFORE UPDATE OR DELETE ON ledger_rejections FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
  TRIGGER ledger_rejections_no_truncate : BEFORE TRUNCATE ON ledger_rejections FOR EACH STATEMENT EXECUTE FUNCTION forbid_mutation()
}

@enduml
